\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Our Father, by whose servants
\par Our house was built of old,
\par Whose hand hath crowned her children
\par With blessings manifold,
\par For Thine unfailing mercies
\par Far-strewn along our way,
\par With all who passed before us,
\par We praise Thy name to- day.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. The changeful years unresting,
\par Their silent course have sped,
\par New comrades' steps to tread:
\par And some are long forgotten,
\par Long spent their hopes and fears;
\par Safe rest they in Thy keeping,
\par Who changest not with years.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. They reap not where they laboured,
\par We reap what they have sown;
\par Our harvest may be garnered
\par By ages yet unknown.
\par The days of old have dowered us
\par With gifts beyond all praise:
\par Our Father, make us faithful
\par To serve the coming days.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Before us and beside us,
\par Still holden in Thine hand,
\par A cloud unseen of witness,
\par Our elder comrades stand:
\par One family unbroken.
\par We join, with one acclaim,
\par One heart, one voice uplifting,
\par To glorify Thy name.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

